"It accepts the same arguments as the [`RetryHandler` "
"constructor](/docs/docs/api/RetryHandler.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:994
msgid "`dump`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:996
msgid ""
"The `dump` interceptor enables you to dump the response body from a "
"request upon a given limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:998 ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1032
#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1152 ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1210
#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1243
msgid "**Options**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:999
msgid ""
"`maxSize` - The maximum size (in bytes) of the response body to dump. If "
"the size of the request's body exceeds this value then the connection "
"will be closed. Default: `1048576`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1001
msgid ""
"The `Dispatcher#options` also gets extended with the options "
"`dumpMaxSize`, `abortOnDumped`, and `waitForTrailers` which can be used "
"to configure the interceptor at a request-per-request basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1003
msgid "**Example - Basic Dump Interceptor**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1026
msgid "`dns`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1028
msgid ""
"The `dns` interceptor enables you to cache DNS lookups for a given "
"duration, per origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1030
msgid ""
"It is well suited for scenarios where you want to cache DNS lookups to "
"avoid the overhead of resolving the same domain multiple times"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1033
msgid ""
"`maxTTL` - The maximum time-to-live (in milliseconds) of the DNS cache. "
"It should be a positive integer. Default: `10000`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1034
msgid "Set `0` to disable TTL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1035
msgid ""
"`maxItems` - The maximum number of items to cache. It should be a "
"positive integer. Default: `Infinity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1036
msgid ""
"`dualStack` - Whether to resolve both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses. Default: "
"`true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1037
msgid ""
"It will also attempt a happy-eyeballs-like approach to connect to the "
"available addresses in case of a connection failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1038
msgid "`affinity` - Whether to use IPv4 or IPv6 addresses. Default: `4`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1039
msgid "It can be either `4` or `6`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1040
msgid "It will only take effect if `dualStack` is `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1041
msgid ""
"`lookup: (hostname: string, options: LookupOptions, callback: (err: "
"NodeJS.ErrnoException | null, addresses: DNSInterceptorRecord[]) => void)"
" => void` - Custom lookup function. Default: `dns.lookup`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1042
msgid ""
"For more info see [dns.lookup](https://nodejs.org/api/dns.html"
"#dnslookuphostname-options-callback)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1043
msgid ""
"`pick: (origin: URL, records: DNSInterceptorRecords, affinity: 4 | 6) => "
"DNSInterceptorRecord` - Custom pick function. Default: `RoundRobin`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1044
msgid "The function should return a single record from the records array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1045
msgid "By default a simplified version of Round Robin is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1046
msgid ""
"The `records` property can be mutated to store the state of the balancing"
" algorithm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1047
msgid "`storage: DNSStorage` - Custom storage for resolved DNS records"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1049
msgid ""
"The `Dispatcher#options` also gets extended with the options "
"`dns.affinity`, `dns.dualStack`, `dns.lookup` and `dns.pick` which can be"
" used to configure the interceptor at a request-per-request basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1052
msgid "**DNSInterceptorRecord** It represents a DNS record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1054
msgid ""
"`family` - (`number`) The IP family of the address. It can be either `4` "
"or `6`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1055
msgid "`address` - (`string`) The IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1057
msgid ""
"**DNSInterceptorOriginRecords** It represents a map of DNS IP addresses "
"records for a single origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1059
msgid "`4.ips` - (`DNSInterceptorRecord[] | null`) The IPv4 addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1060
msgid "`6.ips` - (`DNSInterceptorRecord[] | null`) The IPv6 addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1062
msgid "**DNSStorage** It represents a storage object for resolved DNS records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1064
msgid "`size` - (`number`) current size of the storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1065
msgid ""
"`get` - (`(origin: string) => DNSInterceptorOriginRecords | null`) method"
" to get the records for a given origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1066
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`set` - (`(origin: string, records: DNSInterceptorOriginRecords | null, "
"options: { ttl: number }) => void`) method to set the records for a given"
" origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1067
msgid ""
"`delete` - (`(origin: string) => void`) method to delete records for a "
"given origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1068
msgid ""
"`full` - (`() => boolean`) method to check if the storage is full, if "
"returns `true`, DNS lookup will be skipped in this interceptor and new "
"records will not be stored."
msgstr ""

