msgid "**Example - DNS Interceptor and LRU cache as a storage**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1125
msgid "`responseError`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1127
msgid ""
"The `responseError` interceptor throws an error for responses with status"
" code errors (>= 400)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1129
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1146
msgid "`decompress`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1148
msgid "⚠️ The decompress interceptor is experimental and subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1150
msgid ""
"The `decompress` interceptor automatically decompresses response bodies "
"that are compressed with gzip, deflate, brotli, or zstd compression. It "
"removes the `content-encoding` and `content-length` headers from "
"decompressed responses and supports RFC-9110 compliant multiple "
"encodings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1154
msgid ""
"`skipErrorResponses` - Whether to skip decompression for error responses "
"(status codes >= 400). Default: `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1155
msgid ""
"`skipStatusCodes` - Array of status codes to skip decompression for. "
"Default: `[204, 304]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1157
msgid "**Example - Basic Decompress Interceptor**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1174
msgid "**Example - Custom Options**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1188
msgid "**Supported Encodings**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1190
msgid "`gzip` / `x-gzip` - GZIP compression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1191
msgid "`deflate` / `x-compress` - DEFLATE compression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1192
msgid "`br` - Brotli compression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1193
msgid "`zstd` - Zstandard compression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1194
msgid "Multiple encodings (e.g., `gzip, deflate`) are supported per RFC-9110"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1196
msgid "**Behavior**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1198
msgid "Skips decompression for status codes < 200 or >= 400 (configurable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1199
msgid "Skips decompression for 204 No Content and 304 Not Modified by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1200
msgid "Removes `content-encoding` and `content-length` headers when decompressing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1201
msgid "Passes through unsupported encodings unchanged"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1202
msgid "Handles case-insensitive encoding names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1203
msgid "Supports streaming decompression without buffering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1205
msgid "`Cache Interceptor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1207
msgid ""
"The `cache` interceptor implements client-side response caching as "
"described in [RFC9111](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1212
msgid ""
"`store` - The [`CacheStore`](/docs/docs/api/CacheStore.md) to store and "
"retrieve responses from. Default is "
"[`MemoryCacheStore`](/docs/docs/api/CacheStore.md#memorycachestore)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1213
msgid ""
"`methods` - The [**safe** HTTP methods](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-9.2.1) to cache the response of."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1214
msgid ""
"`cacheByDefault` - The default expiration time to cache responses by if "
"they don't have an explicit expiration and cannot have an heuristic "
"expiry computed. If this isn't present, responses neither with an "
"explicit expiration nor heuristically cacheable will not be cached. "
"Default `undefined`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1215
msgid ""
"`type` - The [type of cache](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/Caching#types_of_caches) for Undici to act as. "
"Can be `shared` or `private`. Default `shared`. `private` implies "
"privately cacheable responses will be cached and potentially shared with "
"other users of your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1217
msgid "**Usage with `fetch`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1239
msgid "`Deduplicate Interceptor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1241
msgid ""
"The `deduplicate` interceptor deduplicates concurrent identical requests."
" When multiple identical requests are made while one is already in-"
"flight, only one request is sent to the origin server, and all waiting "
"handlers receive the same response. This reduces server load and improves"
" performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1245
msgid ""
"`methods` - The [**safe** HTTP methods](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-9.2.1) to deduplicate. Default `['GET']`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1246
msgid ""
"`skipHeaderNames` - Header names that, if present in a request, will "
"cause the request to skip deduplication entirely. Useful for headers like"
" `idempotency-key` where presence indicates unique processing. Header "
"name matching is case-insensitive. Default `[]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1247
msgid ""
"`excludeHeaderNames` - Header names to exclude from the deduplication "
"key. Requests with different values for these headers will still be "
"deduplicated together. Useful for headers like `x-request-id` that vary "
"per request but shouldn't affect deduplication. Header name matching is "
"case-insensitive. Default `[]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1248
msgid ""
"`maxBufferSize` - Maximum bytes buffered per paused waiting deduplicated "
"handler. If a waiting handler remains paused and exceeds this threshold, "
"it is failed with an abort error to prevent unbounded memory growth. "
"Default `5 * 1024 * 1024`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1250
msgid "**Usage**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1268
msgid "Requests are considered identical if they have the same:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1269
msgid "Origin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1270
msgid "HTTP method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1271
msgid "Path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1272
msgid "Request headers (excluding any headers specified in `excludeHeaderNames`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1274
msgid ""
"All deduplicated requests receive the complete response including status "
"code, headers, and body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_Dispatcher.md:1276
msgid ""
"For observability, request deduplication events are published to the "
"`undici:request:pending-requests` [diagnostic "
"channel](/docs/docs/api/DiagnosticsChannel.md#undicirequestpending-"
"requests)."
msgstr ""

